# Train Dense-Keypoint 5 FPS Baseline

This workflow trains the dense-keypoint Social Attention baseline with the
current 5 FPS temporal contract:

```text
source_fps=30
frame_step=6
effective_fps=5
observation_length=16  # 3.2 seconds
prediction_length=24   # 4.8 seconds
window_length=40
```

Thresholds are fit from training windows only. Training and validation windows
are then sampled with the same motion mix:

```text
low=20%, medium=40%, high=40%
score=mean_keypoint_speed_px_s
seed=42
```

## Inspect Dataset and Training Config

Run this before training. It prints the resolved config, motion thresholds,
selected train-window counts, validation-window counts, graph shape, device, and
checkpoint settings without starting optimization.

```sh
python -m train fit --config src/config/train__dense_keypoint_5fps.yml --show-config
```

## Start Training

Use W&B for this experiment so the checkpoint, losses, validation metrics, and
motion-group tables are versioned outside the local workspace.

```sh
python -m train fit --config src/config/train__dense_keypoint_5fps.yml --wandb
```

The CLI prints epoch loss plus a compact validation metric line:

```text
validation_metrics: cFDE=... kFDE=... CVE=... KVE=... BHE=... ROE=...
```

W&B logs every epoch:

- `train/loss`
- `validation/loss`
- scalar validation metrics: `cADE`, `cFDE`, `kADE`, `kFDE`, `CVE`, `KVE`,
  `BHE`, `BFK-ADE`, `BFK-FDE`, `BLE`, `SOE`, `ROE`
- `validation/motion_metrics_table`
- best and periodic model artifacts when checkpointing is enabled

## Compare Against Deterministic Baselines

Run this after training creates
`checkpoints/dense_keypoint_5fps/flat_best.pt`.

```sh
python src/benchmark.py --config src/config/benchmark__dense_keypoint_5fps.yml
```

The comparison writes:

```text
outputs/evaluations/dense_keypoint_5fps/benchmark_16_24/results.jsonl
```

Use this record to compare Social Attention against persistence, rigid constant
velocity, and per-keypoint constant velocity on the same held-out windows.
